# You almost certainly do not need this file.
#
# Auth is `az login`. The server borrows the Azure CLI's token and resolves your
# tenant and default environment from whatever the CLI is signed in to. There is
# nothing to configure and no secret anywhere - the only credential involved is
# the refresh token the Azure CLI already holds.
#
# The one reason to create a .env: targeting a specific environment rather than
# the tenant default.

# Find the GUID in the make.powerautomate.com URL after switching environment.
# Use a DEMO tenant. This server creates, edits and runs real flows.
# PA_ENV_ID=Default-00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
